# Game images (CDN + WebP)

When adding or changing game art under `/static/images/`:

## Python (`app.py`)

- Build paths as `/static/images/{folder}/{name}.webp` (use `Master%20League` for spaced folder names).
- Resolve public URLs with `game_image_public_url()` or `_game_images_webp_path()` + `game_image_public_url()`.
- API JSON must pass image fields through `convert_image_urls()` when returning to the client.
- Do not hardcode absolute CDN hostnames in Python.

## JavaScript (`static/js/app.js`)

- Use `imgUrl(path)` or `imgUrlPreferCdn(path)` for any `/static/images/…` path (handles CDN + WebP).
- For `<img>` tags in generated HTML, prefer `pictureRasterHtml()` so WebP→PNG→`/static` fallback works.
- Do not embed raw `https://…github.io/ggen_db_images/…` URLs in JS.

## Jinja templates (`templates/`)

- Mirror the nav-tab pattern:

```jinja
{% if image_cdn %}{{ image_cdn }}/images/UI/Some_Asset.webp{% else %}/static/images/UI/Some_Asset.webp{% endif %}
```

- Prefer `.webp` filenames. Use `game_images_use_cdn` where a template already gates on both flags (e.g. `game_news.html`).

## Folder lookup

- Confirm the asset folder in `image_index.json` before choosing a path (e.g. `UI_Event_ML_TopRanking` lives under `images/Master League`, not `images/UI`).

## New assets

- Add expected filenames to the CDN repo (`ggen_db_images`) and `image_index.json` when introducing new game images.
